{
  "an4.24:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 4.24 ",
  "an4.24:0.2": "3. At Uruvelā ",
  "an4.24:0.3": "At Kāḷaka’s Monastery ",
  "an4.24:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāketa in Kāḷaka’s monastery. ",
  "an4.24:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "an4.24:1.3": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "an4.24:1.4": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "an4.24:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "an4.24:2.1": "“In this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, its gods and humans—whatever is seen, heard, thought, known, attained, sought, and explored by the mind: that I know. ",
  "an4.24:3.1": "In this world—with its gods, Māras, and divinities, this population with its ascetics and brahmins, its gods and humans—whatever is seen, heard, thought, known, attained, sought, and explored by the mind: that I have insight into. ",
  "an4.24:3.2": "That has been known by a Realized One, but a Realized One is not subject to it. ",
  "an4.24:4.1": "If I were to say that ‘I do not know … the world with its gods’, I would be lying. ",
  "an4.24:5.1": "If I were to say that ‘I both know and do not know … the world with its gods’, that would be just the same. ",
  "an4.24:6.1": "If I were to say that ‘I neither know nor do not know … the world with its gods’, that would be my fault. ",
  "an4.24:7.1": "So a Realized One sees what is to be seen, but does not conceive what is seen, does not conceive what is unseen, does n